   "text": {
    "L1": "A triangle can be linked to a rectangle. The key idea is that its area is half the rectangle's area.",
    "L2": "A diagonal cuts a rectangle into two identical triangles, so each triangle gets exactly half.",
    "L3": "For a 9 centimetre by 6 centimetre rectangle, the rectangle area is 9 times 6, or 54 square centimetres.",
    "L4": "Half of 54 is 27 square centimetres. So the triangle's area is 27 square centimetres.",
    "L5": "For a right-angled triangle, use the two sides that meet at the right angle.",
    "L6": "Do not use the slanted side. Area is half of the product of the two sides around the right angle.",
    "L7": "Now choose the area of the worked-example triangle."
   },
